    "details": "<p><strong>Teams must present an innovative idea, project, prototype, product, or solution addressing a real-world problem.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>The project may be based on areas such as:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning</li>\n<li>Internet of Things (IoT)</li>\n<li>Robotics and Automation</li>\n<li>Cybersecurity</li>\n<li>Sustainable Technology</li>\n<li>Healthcare and Assistive Technology</li>\n<li>Agriculture and Smart Farming</li>\n<li>Education Technology</li>\n<li>Smart City Solutions</li>\n<li>FinTech</li>\n<li>Environmental and Social Innovation</li>\n<li><strong>Any other technology-based innovative solution:</strong>&nbsp;\n<ul>\n<li>The project should demonstrate <strong>originality, creativity, usefulness, and feasibility</strong>.</li>\n<li>Teams are encouraged to demonstrate a <strong>working prototype or proof of concept</strong>, wherever possible.</li>\n<li>Projects that are purely copied or reproduced from existing projects without substantial innovation will not be considered for awards.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>",
